    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

st:auth-42 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MAY ;
    rfc:predicate "Sponsors are created under a platform by users who may create on that platform: any user of the platform-owning organization, SAVVI staff (§4.8), and any user of an org with a **reseller agreement** for the platform (§4.7). There is no per-user create designation. Regardless of who creates it, the sponsor is owned by the platform (AUTH-3). At create time the creator chooses team assignment(s) and the creating org's visibility; after creation, only an **org admin** of that org may change visibility (AUTH-41)." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-42" ;
    au:discipline st:platforms ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

st:auth-50 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST ;
    rfc:predicate "Sponsor ownership is a **two-level hierarchy**. Primary owner: the platform (AUTH-3) / platform-owning organization. Optional subordinate stamp: exactly one **reseller org** (`sponsors.reseller_organization_id`) for reseller-created sponsors (AUTH-44). Ownership is independent of team assignments (AUTH-48)." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-50" ;
    au:discipline st:platforms ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "modality-unstated: the text states no modal verb, so rfc:MUST is a placeholder awaiting a person" .

st:auth-51 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "The reseller stamp confers authority subordinate to the primary owner: - **Grant management** for the sponsor (§4.6), never beyond the reseller org's own granted set. - **Lifecycle management** (archive/offboard, etc.), subject to primary-owner override. - The primary owner may edit/revoke any grant and reassign or clear the stamp. - The stamp is not transferable by the reseller and does not by itself confer sponsor permissions — access still flows through the §4.6 grant and the reseller's own teams." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-51" ;
    au:discipline st:platforms ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

