st:auth-43 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "A **platform admin** or **SAVVI admin** may establish a **reseller agreement** between a platform and another WorkOS Organization. **Platform admins** may add a reseller **only by name and domain** (reuse the WorkOS Organization that owns the domain, or create and mirror one); they must not be offered an organization picker that would disclose other platforms' reseller partners. **SAVVI admins** may add by selecting an existing mirrored organization **or** by name and domain. Webhooks never invent agreements. The agreement confers `sponsor:create` (AUTH-42) and specifies a platform-owned **book team** and default **grant permission set** (typically `{sponsor:edit}`). Platform admins see only their agreements; SAVVI admins may manage any platform's." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-43" ;
    au:discipline st:resellers ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

