st:auth-61 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "Tasks carry their own visibility (`public` default / `restricted` / `private`), orthogonal to sponsor access. A task's **participants** — assignee, delegate, and subscribers — always see it in full detail, even without any permission on its sponsor. Non-participants need `sponsor:view` on the parent sponsor and see: | Task visibility | Participant | `sponsor:view` non-participant | | ------------------ | ----------- | ------------------------------ | | `public` (default) | full | full | | `restricted` | full | attributes only | | `private` | full | not-found (AUTH-17) | The attributes projection is an allowlist (title, type, status, priority, dates, assignment, hierarchy) — never description or comments. Full-detail access gates comments and related task operations." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-61" ;
    au:discipline st:tasks ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

st:auth-62 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "Plan-year **documents** require `sponsor:view` via the parent sponsor (AUTH-16). Task-comment **attachments** are a distinct document kind and follow the visibility of the task whose comment carries them: full-detail access to that task is required; document rules never apply. S3 upload and download tokens are issued only after these same checks." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-62" ;
    au:discipline st:tasks ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

st:auth-63 a rfc:NormativeStatement ;
    rfc:modality rfc:MUST_NOT ;
    rfc:predicate "A user's **collaborating organizations** are: their own org, the platform-owning org and every grant-holding org of each sponsor in their org's pool, and SAVVI (AUTH-23). The user directory lists active members of collaborating orgs only (default scope) or own-org members only (team pickers, AUTH-6); an all-users scope is SAVVI-staff-only. The directory is never a vehicle to enumerate unrelated organizations' users." ;
    rdfs:label "AUTH-63" ;
    au:discipline st:directory ;
    au:rung au:R0 ;
    au:stalledOn "not-decomposed: modality was pattern-matched from the claim text and nobody has confirmed it; no terms grounded, so nothing can be checked yet" .

